From 2f78a93a29dc4816040cfb909f8b1440000c7608 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 10:07:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] feat(theme): material colours of the classic artwork read
 --odon-rest-*/--odon-fill-*

The measured donors in tools/toothgen/source already wrap their material
fills and gradient stops in --odon-rest-* / --odon-fill-* variables; the six
classic runtime templates hard-coded them, so a host could not recolour a
zircon crown or the metal-ceramic ramp under the default anatomy.

Each classic material colour is now var(--odon-<same name as the donor>,
<classic colour>): the line-aligned donor gives the variable, the classic
file keeps its own colour as the fallback, so the default rendering is
unchanged (596 attributes, matched by element id).

README: documents the material variables.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
